# Extensibility — {{id}}

Generated by creation mode. This document is the human-readable half of the
machine contract in `extensibility.json`.

## Surface

- Kind: `webview` (a page at `/plugins/{{id}}/`, plus a Native chunk)
- Tool: `{{tool}}` (published as `{{publishedTool}}`)
- Chunk: `ui/settings.js` contributes to `keel.ui.settings-section`
  (form `chunk`, same host VM, host theme tokens, TUI-compatible)
- Page: `ui/index.html` via `provides.ui.entry`

## How to use it

1. `creation validate {id: "{{id}}"}` — field-level problems, fail closed.
2. `creation install {id: "{{id}}"}` — durable approval, then install + enable.
3. The panel appears under Settings › Plugins; the tool appears in the tool
   surface once the plugin is enabled.
4. `creation remove {id: "{{id}}"}` — uninstall, then the staged package and
   every contribution are withdrawn.

## Attachment previews (optional)

To render message attachments, contribute to `keel.ui.message-part` and claim
the attachment part in `extensibility.json`:

```json
{ "slot": "keel.ui.message-part", "form": "chunk", "entry": "ui/preview.js",
  "part": "attachment", "mime": ["application/pdf", "image/*"] }
```

- `mime` is `type/subtype` or `type/*` (lowercase, at most 32 patterns per
  contribution). Omit it to claim every attachment MIME.
- One plugin may not claim the same MIME pattern twice; across plugins the host
  picks the first declared match in slot order (first declaration wins).
- The renderer receives metadata and same-origin URLs only — never bytes. Keep
  the file name, size and download/open entry visible.
- Disable/uninstall withdraws the preview in the same generation.

## Boundaries

- UI talks to the host only through `keel.plugin.*`; it never receives a secret.
- Permissions are declared in `plugin.yaml` and enforced at dispatch.
- An undeclared tool is refused and audited; an unapproved install never runs.
